# ============================================================================================
# tri_rgba — barycentric attribute interpolation (3D arc rung 11)
# ============================================================================================
# ⛔ GENERATED, NOT HAND-WRITTEN. Produced by `scripts/check/shader-blob.sh emit kernel/shaders/tri_rgba.s
# tri_rgba` from the assembler's own output, and gated by `scripts/check/shader-blob.sh check` so it can
# never drift from the source. Editing a dword here by hand is how a table and its .s file diverge
# silently: the kernel still builds and the failure surfaces on iron as a wedged queue or a wrong
# picture with nothing pointing back at the cause.
# ⚠ RSRC1 = 0x002C0187 (32 VGPRs, 56 SGPRs), RSRC2 = 0x00000190 — both HARVESTED from the assembled
# descriptor, never counted. RSRC2 is byte-identical to the coverage kernel's, which is what lets
# the shipped dispatcher issue this blob with no PM4 change.
# ⚠ ONE ASSEMBLER SO FAR. The standing bar is two independent ones (see the note above
# edge_setup_write); the sovereign edgeasm re-emit is a separate bite and this blob must not reach
# a hardware run before it lands.
fn tri_rgba_write(dst_phys) {
    store32(dst_phys + 0,    0xbefe01c1);
    store32(dst_phys + 4,    0x8e0a8608);
    store32(dst_phys + 8,    0x6802000a);
    store32(dst_phys + 12,   0x7d980206);
    store32(dst_phys + 16,   0xbe94206a);
