# tex_bilin_write — the RUNG 15 BILINEAR blob, 584 dwords, emitted by scripts/check/shader-blob.sh
# from kernel/shaders/tex_bilin.s. ⚠ NEVER hand-edit: `sh scripts/check/shader-blob.sh check
# kernel/shaders/tex_bilin.s tex_bilin` diffs this table against the assembled source, and check.sh
# runs it on every build.
#
# ⭐ 584 = 442 (rung 13) + 142. The added dwords are the four-tap fetch, the per-channel integer
# blend; NOTHING in rung 13's head or tail changed. That is not a claim, it is a GATE —
# scripts/check/texbi-body-identity.sh proves the head span (99 source lines) and the tail span (75
# source lines, 73 dwords) are character- and byte-identical to tex_rgba.s, and asserts that the only
# dword differences in the head are branch OFFSETS carrying the same SOPP opcode.
#
# ⚠ THIS BLOB IS 48-VGPR. It MUST be dispatched with GPU_COMPUTE_PGM_RSRC1_TEXBI, never RSRC1_TEX.
# Dispatching a 48-VGPR kernel under a 32-VGPR declaration does not fault — it silently aliases the
# high registers across waves, which on this silicon is a wrong picture, not a wedge, and therefore
# the hardest possible thing to attribute. gpu_tex_dispatch picks both the slot and the descriptor
# from the same `bilin` flag so the two cannot be set inconsistently.
